# Skill: feature-harness

Read and follow `skills/feature-harness/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/feature-harness/templates/what-was-run.md` only (inner skills fill their own files).

Announce: `Using skill: feature-harness`. Then announce each inner skill.

## Job

Run `feature-developer`, `feature-code-reviewer`, `feature-verifier` in order for one feature specification. One verify-fail retry. Stop after that. Classify later feedback; new product goes to specifier first.

## When

Operator wants the path, a harness, or end-to-end, and a specification exists (or they are sending feedback on a folder that already ran).

## Must (order)

1. Resolve the feature folder. No specification → stop, name `feature-specifier`. Empty kitchen → stop, no scaffold.
2. Execute each inner `SKILL.md`. Do not skip review. Wait on inner questions.
3. Verify fail → one more develop → review → verify, then stop if still fail.
4. Cancel → halt, write the log.
5. Feedback: spec-mismatch → path. New product → specifier then path. Unsure → ask.
6. Write `docs/features/<name>/what-was-run.md`.

## Must not

- Automation, SDK, CLI daemon, CI, queue UI
- Scaffold a stack
- Skip review
- Auto-specifier when there is no specification and no product-feedback message
- Recode extra product as a developer fix
